id: pm-gh1726
title: "GH-1726: a strict boolean extension flag accepts an empty array from direct callers (PmClient.run, the test harness), while {} and 1 are refused"
description: "GH-1726 (filed 2026-11-14). A flag declared value_type boolean with value_validation strict accepts an empty array from direct callers: PmClient.run and the extension test harness's runCommand. The handler receives options.enabled === [] (typeof object) with no warning, while {}, 'bogus' and 1 are refused before dispatch with extension_flag_value_invalid (exit 2). A handler that trusts the host's strict validation, which 2026.11.8+ encourages because the host owns option spelling and value checks, can therefore read a truthy object where it expects true or false. Likely cause from the issue: the empty array is taken as 'no repeated values' and validation is skipped. Expected: a non-repeatable flag never accepts an array; a repeatable boolean flag validates each element and refuses an empty array where at least one value is required. The issue also asks that the changelog name the direct-caller string coercion ('true' -> true) for strict booleans, which broke several fleet test suites between 2026.11.7 and 2026.11.9. Duplicate check: searched strict boolean extension flag empty array direct caller; no open item."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: extensions,flags,"gh:1726",sdk,validation
created_at: "2026-11-14T09:00:39.423Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T19:43:19.365Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-14T19:16:20.807Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-14T19:16:20.807Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A strict boolean flag refuses [] from PmClient.run and the test harness with extension_flag_value_invalid, exit 2, before dispatch; A non-repeatable flag refuses any array and a repeatable boolean flag validates every element; Specs cover [], {}, 1, 'bogus' and 'true' for both direct callers and the CLI"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: high
reporter: unbraind
severity: medium
resolution: "normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions (src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts) refuses an array for a flag that is not list/repeatable with extension_flag_value_invalid (flag field) and treats an empty required list as missing; a raw repeatable declaration counts as list. applyDynamicExtensionFlagOptions (src/cli/extension-command-help.ts) records each bare repeatable switch occurrence as true. optionsWithAuthor (src/sdk/runtime-input.ts) skips the native-field array rewrites for extension actions (nativeAction: false from runtime.ts dispatchAction). Strict scalar refusals carry flag. pm-g2zzus owns the mixed attached/bare ordering edge."
expected_result: "A strict boolean refuses [], [true], {}, 1 and 'bogus' from PmClient.run and the harness before dispatch; 'true' still coerces; a repeatable boolean validates each element; pm <cmd> --many delivers [true]"
actual_result: "direct-caller-option-contract.integration.spec and command-options.spec pass for both direct callers and the in-process CLI; --many -> [true], --many --many -> [true, true]; linked run passed 34/34"
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
